  "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}-\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}-\\frac{6\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(6)\u2248{80.538}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince ${80.538}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={80.538}^{\u2218}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract ${180}^{\u2218}$ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={80.538}^{\u2218}-{180}^{\u2218}\u2248-{99.462}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $80.538\\cdot (-99.462)\u2248-8\\,010.$",
